lumn (0,0) and full 1e-6 elsewhere. \n\nFor the test, I need to construct a NonlinearRotatingMPCMap entry with master rotations at that boundary value. How do master rotations come from u? `entry.master_rotations(u)` extracts theta from u via projections. Building a full model to achieve master rotations of pi-1.5e-6... The r4 test builds q with rotations up to 0.35 rad — not near pi. To get master thetas near pi, I'd need u with rotation dofs ~ pi. That's fine — I can directly construct u: the map's master_theta_projs map reduced/global dofs... Actually `master_rotations(u)` — let me check: entry.master_rotations(u) at line 1397. It probably computes theta_i = P_i @ u or from full u dofs. If I set the master rotation dofs in u to (pi-1.5e-6,0,0), the entry's masters get those thetas.\n\nBut wait — will `geometric_tangent` be reached with such u? The test can call `mpc_map.geometric_tangent(u, imbalance)` directly with a synthetic u (like the r4 test does with full_u(q)). I need:\n- u admitted for the map (master rotations within chart): (pi-1.5e-6,0,0) < pi-1e-6 ✓.\n- imbalance with nonzero f_b and m_b at the slave dofs.\n- projs with nnz > 0 (rotational projections) — true for the interpolated/eccentric cantilever map.\n\nThen:\n1. Discriminating check: the OLD fixed-h stencil would raise — demonstrate by calling `_so3_weighted_mean` on the plus probe directly and asserting SO3MeanDomainError (proves the probe is outside the domain, i.e., the regression is discriminating).\n2. New behavior: `K = mpc_map.geometric_tangent(u, imbalance)` returns a finite sparse matrix without raising.\n3. Correctness: compare against a reference: central differences of the covector map with a manually-safe h (e.g., 1e-8, admitted for all probes here since pi-1.5e-6+1e-8 < pi-1e-6). Compute reference D blocks via the same internal formula? That duplicates internals. Alternative: compare `geometric_tangent(u, imbalance)` against finite differences of `reduce_force`-like covector map..